---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Now from "@/components/Now.astro";
import { level, xp } from "@/data/level";
---

<Layout title="Pavel Kleisner - Senior Backend Engineer, Team Lead & AI Tooling">

    <section class="hero">
        <img class="avatar" src="/pavel.jpg" alt="Pavel Kleisner" width="300" height="300" />
        <div>
            <p class="kicker">Senior backend engineer · team lead · AI tooling · <b>level {level}</b></p>
            <h1>Pavel Kleisner</h1>
            <p class="sub">I build and look after backend systems in Kotlin, Java, Spring and PostgreSQL: integrations, releases and production issues. I also build small tools that let AI agents work with real systems.</p>
            <div class="actions">
                <a class="btn" href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
                <a href="/projects/">Projects and experience</a>
            </div>
            <nav class="jump" aria-label="On this page">
                <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
                <a href="#ai">AI tooling</a>
                <a href="#stack">Tech stack</a>
            </nav>
        </div>
    </section>

    <dl class="sheet" aria-label="Character sheet">
        <div><dt>Class</dt><dd>Backend engineer / AI tooling</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Level</dt><dd>{level} years in production</dd><dd class="xp" title={`${xp} % to level ${level + 1}`}><span style={`width:${xp}%`}></span></dd></div>
        <div><dt>Home base</dt><dd>Near Prague, remote</dd></div>
        <div class="lfg"><dt>Party status</dt><dd>Open to contracts</dd></div>
    </dl>

    <div class="book">
        <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
            <p>On this page</p>
            <a href="#experience">Experience</a>
            <a href="#skills">What I do</a>
            <a href="#ai">AI tooling</a>
            <a href="#story">From production</a>
            <a href="#stack">Tech stack</a>
            <a href="#now">Right now</a>
        </nav>

        <div>
            <section class="chapter" id="experience">
                <h2>Experience</h2>
                <div class="quests">
                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-main">Main quest</span><h3>TSM / CETIN</h3><span class="when">2020 – now</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Senior backend and integration engineer, team lead</p>
                        <div class="quest-body split">
                            <p>Kotlin and Java services on PostgreSQL for a telco operator's service platform: B2B flows, change management, partner integrations and incident analysis.</p>
                            <ul class="objectives">
                                <li>Led the 2.2 production rollout</li>
                                <li>Leading the 2.4 rollout and its release batches</li>
                                <li>Core developer on version 1.5</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </article>
                    <article class="quest">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-side">Side quest</span><h3>Nordic web</h3><span class="when">2024 – now, on demand</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Ongoing work on a Django web application, focused changes when they're needed.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="quest past">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-done">Completed</span><h3>MNCP</h3><span class="when">2018 – 2021</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Full-stack Kotlin/Spring and Angular: authentication, exports, archives, measurement batches.</p>
                    </article>
                    <article class="quest past">
                        <div class="quest-head"><span class="badge b-done">Completed</span><h3>ZIS</h3><span class="when">2017 – 2018</span></div>
                        <p class="role">Enterprise Java and ZK. Where I learned to deliver a feature end to end.</p>
                    </article>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="skills">
                <h2>What I do</h2>
                <dl class="rows">
                    <div><dt>Integrations</dt><dd>B2B APIs, message contracts, retries and the failure modes that only show up once a partner system is connected.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Releases</dt><dd>New platform versions into real environments: old data, backward compatibility, rollout order and a way back.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Debugging production</dt><dd>Logs, metrics, the database and domain knowledge together, until the cause is clear.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Architecture</dt><dd>Small safe changes, clearly named rules and sensible service boundaries.</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="ai">
                <h2><span class="badge b-party">Companion</span> AI tooling</h2>
                <p>I use AI agents every day and build small tools that let them work with real systems. They explore unfamiliar code, draft routine parts, run tests and review a diff before I do.</p>
                <dl class="rows">
                    <div><dt>Own MCP servers</dt><dd>Read-only log search over Elasticsearch with server-side guards and an audit log (working prototype), a Jira server, and a team-chat bridge that only sends a message after I confirm the draft.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Skills and shared context</dt><dd>One knowledge base for Claude Code and Codex, and a library of repeatable workflows: preparing a release batch, scanning container images, fixing a ticket in an isolated branch.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Ground rules</dt><dd>Agents only read production data, I push to git myself, every data fix ships with a revert script, and credentials reach MCP servers through environment variables or a separate form, never through the chat.</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Side projects</dt><dd>Built mostly by agents. That's where I learn what they can be trusted with.</dd></div>
                </dl>
                <p style="margin-top:1.2rem">I review every change before it ships, check its behaviour with tests or in the running app, and I'm accountable for the result.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="story">
                <h2><span class="badge b-boss">Boss fight</span> The UUID that wasn't a UUID</h2>
                <p>When we rolled out the first platform version, the integration spec said the <code>messageId</code> would be a UUID. One partner started failing straight away: their system had been quietly parsing the ticket ID out of the old <code>ticketId_timestamp</code> format, even though the ticket ID sat right there in the message body.</p>
                <p>The clean fix was on their side, but in a corporate setting it would have taken months. So I switched our side back to the old format and production kept running.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="stack">
                <h2>Tech stack</h2>
                <dl class="skills">
                    <div><dt>Main</dt><dd>Kotlin, Java, Spring, PostgreSQL, Kafka</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>AI tooling</dt><dd>Claude Code, Codex, MCP servers, agent skills</dd></div>
                    <div><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kubernetes, Oracle, Angular, Python and Django, TypeScript, Astro</dd></div>
                </dl>
            </section>

            <section class="chapter" id="now">
                <h2>Right now</h2>
                <Now lang="en" />
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>

    <section class="party">
        <div>
            <h2>Need a backend engineer?</h2>
            <p>Long-term or focused contracts: backend systems, integrations, production releases and tooling for AI agents.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:contact@pavelkleisner.dev">contact@pavelkleisner.dev</a>
    </section>

</Layout>
